## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to combine streaming sketches with efficient top-K data structures while reasoning about accuracy, space, and time trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- **Streaming Algorithms:** Processing unbounded data with limited memory
- **Count-Min Sketch (CMS):** Probabilistic data structure for frequency estimation with false positives but no false negatives
- **Top-K Maintenance:** Using a min-heap to track the K most frequent elements efficiently
- **Amortized Analysis:** Bounding average cost over sequences of operations
- **Space-Time Trade-offs:** Comparing approximate vs. exact approaches

## Code Example
```javascript
class CountMinSketch {
  constructor(w, d) {
    this.w = w;
    this.d = d;
    this.table = Array.from({ length: d }, () => Array(w).fill(0));
  }

  hash(key, i) {
    const str = typeof key === 'string' ? key : String(key);
    let hash = 0;
    for (let j = 0; j < str.length; j++) {
      hash = (hash * 31 + str.charCodeAt(j)) >>> 0;
    }
    return (hash + i * 31) % this.w;
  }

  update(key) {
    for (let i = 0; i < this.d; i++) {
      const j = this.hash(key, i);
      this.table[i][j]++;
    }
  }

  estimate(key) {
    let min = Infinity;
    for (let i = 0; i < this.d; i++) {
      const j = this.hash(key, i);
      min = Math.min(min, this.table[i][j]);
    }
    return min;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests sliding-window frequency tracking with fixed memory and per-element updates, a common real-time pattern in fraud/rate-limiting use cases. It also shows practical data-structure trade-offs for beginners.

## Key Concepts
- Sliding window with fixed memory
- Circular buffer + hashmap for frequencies
- Per-element O(1) updates; batch O(B)
- Threshold tracking to avoid full scans
- Choosing W, r, B depends on latency and memory constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
class SlidingWindowCounter {
  constructor(W) {
    this.W = W;
    this.buf = new Array(W);
    this.head = 0;
    this.size = 0;
    this.freq = new Map();
    this.crossed = 0; // number of IDs currently crossing the threshold
  }
  processBatch(batch, r) {
    for (const id of batch) {
      // increment
      const c = this.freq.get(id) || 0;
      const nc = c + 1;
      this.freq.set(id, nc);
      if (nc === r) this.crossed++;
      // push to circular buffer
      const idx = (this.head + this.size) % this.W;
      this.buf[idx] = id;
      if (this.size < this.W) {
        this.size++;
      } else {
        // evict oldest
        const old = this.buf[this.head];
        this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.W;
        const co = this.freq.get(old) || 0;
        const nco = co - 1;
        if (nco <= 0) this.freq.delete(old);
        else this.freq.set(old, nco);
        if (co >= r && nco < r) this.crossed--;
      }
    }
    return this.crossed > 0;
  }
}
```

